<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's Bank of Punjab 6.98 pct up.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's Bank of Punjab 6.98 pct up.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Punjab rose 2.25 rupees, or 6.98 percent, to 34.50 in early trade on fresh buying by investors from Punjab, the home province of Pakistan's new Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 62,500 shares were traded early at the Karachi Stock Exchange amid expectations that Bank of Punjab will announce higher profits for calendar 1996, one dealer said.</p>
<p>The bank paid 30 percent bonus stocks for calendar 1995. It has not said when it will announce its annual results.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
